ices went up because steel makers need more."], "note": ""}, {"en": "feuilletonist", "uk": "фейлетоніст", "pos": "noun", "band": "rare", "share": null, "raw_rank": null, "meaning_hint": "", "examples": ["The feuilletonist wrote a funny column about city traffic.", "Every Sunday, the feuilletonist shared light stories in the newspaper.", "As a feuilletonist, he wrote short essays about daily life.", "Readers loved the feuilletonist's jokes about local politicians."], "note": "Rare; \"columnist\" is the common word."}, {"en": "fibrilla", "uk": "фібрила", "pos": "noun", "band": "rare", "share": null, "raw_rank": null, "meaning_hint": "", "examples": ["A fibrilla is a very thin thread inside a cell.", "Under the microscope, you can see each fibrilla in the muscle.", "Muscle fibers are made of many small fibrillae.", "The teacher drew a fibrilla on the board for the class."], "note": "Plural: fibrillae. \"Fibril\" is more common."}, {"en": "fibrinoid", "uk": "фібриноїд", "pos": "noun", "band": "rare", "share": null, "raw_rank": null, "meaning_hint": "", "examples": ["The doctor found fibrinoid in the walls of small blood vessels.", "Fibrinoid can appear in tissue when there is inflammation.", "The lab report mentioned fibrinoid in the kidney sample.", "Fibrinoid looks pink under the microscope after staining."], "note": ""}, {"en": "fibrinolysin", "uk": "фібринолізин", "pos": "noun", "band": "rare", "share": null, "raw_rank": null, "meaning_hint": "", "examples": ["Fibrinolysin is an enzyme that breaks down blood clots.", "The body makes fibrinolysin to keep blood flowing.", "Doctors sometimes use fibrinolysin to clean wounds.", "Scientists measured fibrinolysin levels in the blood samples."], "note": ""}, {"en": "fibrocement", "uk": "фіброцемент", "pos": "noun", "band": "rare", "share": null, "raw_rank": null, "meaning_hint": "", "examples": ["We covered the roof with fibrocement sheets.", "Fibrocement siding is strong and does not burn easily.", "The builder cut the fibrocement boards for the new fence.", "Fibrocement panels are popular for outside walls."], "note": "Often called \"fiber cement\" in American English."}, {"en": "fibrocyte", "uk": "фіброцит", "pos": "noun", "band": "rare", "share": null, "raw_rank": null, "meaning_hint": "", "examples": ["A fibrocyte is a resting cell in connective tissue.", "Fibrocytes can become active when the skin is hurt.", "The biology book shows a fibrocyte next to other cells.", "Researchers study how fibrocytes help wounds heal."], "note": ""}, {"en": "fibrolipoma", "uk": "фіброліпома", "pos": "noun", "band": "rare", "share": null, "raw_rank": null, "meaning_hint": "", "examples": ["The doctor said the soft lump was a fibrolipoma.", "A fibrolipoma is a harmless growth of fat and tissue.", "She had a small fibrolipoma removed from her back.", "The scan showed a fibrolipoma, so there was no need to worry."], "note": ""}, {"en": "fibrolite", "uk": "фіброліт", "pos": "noun", "band": "rare", "share": null, "raw_rank": null, "meaning_hint": "", "examples": ["Fibrolite is a mineral that forms thin, hair-like crystals.", "The geologist found fibrolite in the old metamorphic rock.", "This white stone sample is called fibrolite.", "Fibrolite is also known as sillimanite."], "note": ""}, {"en": "fibromyoma", "uk": "фіброміома", "pos": "noun", "band": "rare", "share": null, "raw_rank": null, "meaning_hint": "", "examples": ["The doctor found a small fibromyoma in her uterus.", "A fibromyoma is usually not cancer.", "She had surgery to remove the fibromyoma last year.", "Many women with a fibromyoma have no symptoms at all."], "note": "The everyday word is \"fibroid\"."}, {"en": "fictionalism", "uk": "фікціоналізм", "pos": "noun", "band": "rare", "share": null, "raw_rank": null, "meaning_hint": "", "examples": ["Fictionalism says some ideas are useful stories, not real things.", "In philosophy class, we discussed fictionalism about numbers.", "Her paper argues for fictionalism in math.", "Fictionalism is a hard idea for first-year students."], "note": ""}, {"en": "figurant", "uk": "фігурант", "pos": "noun", "band": "rare", "share": null, "raw_rank": null, "meaning_hint": "", "examples": ["The police named him a figurant in the fraud case.", "Each figurant in the case must answer the court's questions.", "The newspaper listed every figurant in the bribery investigation.", "She became a figurant after the documents were found."], "note": "Rare in English; \"suspect\" or \"person of interest\" is common."}, {"en": "finalism", "uk": "фіналізм", "pos": "noun", "band": "rare", "share": null, "raw_rank": null, "meaning_hint": "", "examples": ["Finalism is the idea that nature has goals.", "The professor explained finalism in our biology history lecture.", "Many scientists reject finalism because evolution has no aim.", "His book criticizes finalism in old ideas about life."], "note": ""}, {"en": "finitism", "uk": "фінітизм", "pos": "noun", "band": "rare", "share": null, "raw_rank": null, "meaning_hint": "", "examples": ["Finitism accepts only math objects that can be built in steps.", "Our math teacher explained finitism with simple examples.", "Finitism does not accept infinite sets as real.", "She wrote her thesis on finitism and logic."], "note": ""}, {"en": "fioritura", "uk": "фіоритура", "pos": "noun", "band": "rare", "share": null, "raw_rank": null, "meaning_hint": "", "examples": ["The singer added a beautiful fioritura at the end of the song.", "This opera aria is full of difficult fioritura.", "The teacher showed me how to sing a short fioritura.", "Too much fioritura can hide the main melody."], "note": "Plural: fioriture."}, {"en": "fistball", "uk": "фістбол", "pos": "noun", "band": "rare", "share": null, "raw_rank": null, "meaning_hint": "", "examples": ["Fistball is like volleyball, but you hit the ball with your fist.", "Our school started a fistball team this year.", "We played fistball in the park after work.", "Fistball is very popular in Germany and Austria."], "note": ""}, {"en": "fixage", "uk": "фіксаж", "pos": "noun", "band": "rare", "share": null, "raw_rank": null, "meaning_hint": "", "examples": ["After developing the photo, put it in the fixage bath.", "Fixage stops the photo from changing in the light.", "Don't skip fixage, or your prints will turn dark.", "The darkroom has trays for developer, stop bath, and fixage."], "note": "Rare; photographers usually say \"fixing\" or \"fixer\"."}, {"en": "flaperon", "uk": "флаперон", "pos": "noun", "band": "rare", "share": null, "raw_rank": null, "meaning_hint": "", "examples": ["The pilot moved the flaperon to slow the small plane.", "A flaperon works as both a flap and an aileron.", "The mechanic checked the flaperon on the right wing.", "Part of a plane's flaperon was found on the beach."], "note": ""}, {"en": "flavopurpurin", "uk": "флавопурпурин", "pos": "noun", "band": "rare", "share": null, "raw_rank": null, "meaning_hint": "", "examples": ["Flavopurpurin is a red dye used for fabrics.", "In the past, factories used flavopurpurin to color cotton.", "The chemist made flavopurpurin in the lab.", "This old cloth was dyed with flavopurpurin."], "note": ""}, {"en": "flerovium", "uk": "флеровій", "pos": "noun", "band": "rare", "share": null, "raw_rank": null, "meaning_hint": "", "examples": ["Flerovium is a very heavy element made in a lab.", "Flerovium has the symbol Fl and number 114.", "Scientists made only a few atoms of flerovium.", "Flerovium breaks down in just a few seconds."], "note": ""}, {"en": "flibustier", "uk": "флібустьєр", "pos": "noun", "band": "rare", "share": null, "raw_rank": null, "meaning_hint": "", "examples": ["The flibustier attacked ships in the Caribbean Sea.", "The movie is about a brave flibustier and his crew.", "Each flibustier hoped to find gold on Spanish ships.", "My son wants to dress as a flibustier for the party."], "note": "Old word; \"pirate\" or \"buccaneer\" is common. Also \"filibuster\"."}, {"en": "focometer", "uk": "фо